e, a lethal fetal anomaly, and rape or incest up to 10 weeks.\n- **What the vote shows:** a No on a ban puts him on the side against banning, which is also not near-unanimous. It does not say whether he would allow abortion at every stage, through the second trimester, or only the first. Rungs 1–3 all differ on those clauses, so the vote can't choose between them.\n- **The forum transcript (2026):** these are his own words, but they cover democracy, the economy, energy, LGBTQ issues and redistricting. Nothing in it is about abortion, so I coded it `off`.\n\n**How the four passages are coded:**\n\n| Source | Coded as | Fields filled |\n|---|---|---|\n| Roll call | `record` / `vote` | `actor_quote` \"Eberhart Jackson Pierce\", `tally_quote` \"Yea 62 Abortion Nay 38 Excused 0 Not Voting 0\" |\n| Enrolled bill text | `record` / `vote` | `provision_quote` (the \"criminal act, except…\" clause) |\n| Bill-details page | `record` / `vote` | no quotes; it has only the digest and doesn't show his action |\n| Forum transcript | `off`, `statement-other` | none |\n\n**Two judgement calls to check:**\n- I dated the forum passage `2026` only. The source gives two dates (2026-06-09 on On the Record, 2026-03-23 in the file name).\n- I coded the bill-details page as a record passage on the same instrument rather than leaving it out.\n\n**`needs_source` lists two things:**\n- Pierce's own words on gestational limits or exceptions, such as a questionnaire, an issue page, or a floor speech or explanation of his SB 1(ss) vote.\n- Any amendment roll call on SB 1(ss) that set a specific limit or exception and that he voted on.","ttft_ms":12776,"type":"result","duration_ms":37065,"uuid":"87893a87-9545-4444-a0df-89e5d6985f0d","ttft_stream_ms":2282,"time_to_request_ms":395,"first_content_frame_ms":2282,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
